    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Role: You are an expert data analyst specializing in Postgresql/EnterprisedDB Advanced Server 9.6 monitoring and performance optimization.\n\nInput: Using “task breakdown” tool, analyze the provided Postgresql/EnterprisedDB Advanced Server 9.6 monitoring metrics. Use the summary and trimmed details below.\n\n**Server Summary:**\n- Server: {{ $json.body.summary.server }}\n- Timestamp: {{ $json.body.summary.timestamp }}\n- Service Status: {{ $json.body.summary.service_status }}\n- Connection Status: {{ $json.body.summary.connection_status }}\n- Disk Usage: {{ $json.body.summary.disk_usage_percent }}%\n- Load (1min): {{ $json.body.summary.load_avg_1min }}\n- Memory Used: {{ $json.body.summary.memory_used_percent }}%\n- Connections: total {{ $json.body.summary.total_connections }}, active {{ $json.body.summary.active_connections }}\n- Cache Hit Ratio: {{ $json.body.summary.cache_hit_ratio }}%\n- Deadlocks: {{ $json.body.summary.deadlocks }}\n- Connected Replicas: {{ $json.body.summary.connected_replicas }}\n- Archive Mode: {{ $json.body.summary.archive_mode }}\n\n**Alerts:**\n{{ JSON.stringify($json.body.alerts ?? [], null, 2) }}\n\n**Storage Summary:**\n{{ JSON.stringify($json.body.storage_summary ?? {}, null, 2) }}\n\n**Selected Detailed Metrics (trimmed):**\n{{ JSON.stringify({\n  system: $json.body.system,\n  performance: $json.body.performance,\n  database: $json.body.database,\n  locks: {\n    waiting_sessions: $json.body.locks?.waiting_sessions,\n    top_waiters: ($json.body.locks?.top_waiters ?? []).slice(0, 5),\n    blocking_chains: ($json.body.locks?.blocking_chains ?? []).slice(0, 5)\n  },\n  vacuum: {\n    top_dead_tuples: ($json.body.vacuum?.top_dead_tuples ?? []).slice(0, 10)\n  },\n  wal: $json.body.wal,\n  replication: $json.body.replication,\n  backup: $json.body.backup,\n  bloat: $json.body.bloat,\n  configuration: $json.body.configuration\n}, null, 2) }}\n\nSteps:\n1. Identify the top 3–7 most important issues from the metrics.\n2. If you need historical context, use the Knowledge Base Retriever tool at most once.\n3. Synthesize the real-time metrics with any retrieved context.\n4. Assess security risks and compliance issues based on the data.\n5. Evaluate backup and recovery readiness.\n6. Prioritize issues according to their business impact (Critical, High, Medium, Low).\n7. Enumerate all issues identified and important information about each issue. Make a list of issues and format the list using the Parser tool.\n8. For each issue identified, provide title, priority, brief description, Remediation Steps, preventative actions, and proactive monitoring improvements.\n9. Remove duplicates\n\nExpectation: Use Structured Output Parser tool to format the output. As an output, produce a list of all issues derived from input metrics after analysis. Each issue on the list should have a unique title, derived priority, a brief issue description, identified remediation steps to resolve the identified issue, and realistic preventive actions and monitoring improvements to avoid issue recurrence.\n",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {}
      },
